{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791745945,"nonce":"jYGgtJMpAbgFoeO3tg8p3S+3S3g=","message":"Scene serialization exposed a cost of disabling TLAB for precise allocation accounting. This is an observation to investigate, not a confirmed leak or a measured memory-pressure trend.\n\nUsing the local release at source 778a2094, default hybrid --preset game, ChimpMonk SceneFileBench (typed scene codec versus compact Haxe JSON) normally completed in three guarded fresh processes with sampled group RSS 198.1, 197.2 and 195.6 MiB. Logs: 3svw50s5, p7ues5s9, xci_zbiy in the ChimpMonk benchmark TMPDIR.\n\nA single ASH_GC_TLAB=0 attempt with the same artifact reached 557.4 MiB before the 512 MiB guard stopped it (5w11aezb). No timing from that stopped attempt is used. Command: python3 -B scripts/bench.py --timeout 60 -- env ASH_GC_TLAB=0 ../ash/target/release/ash --preset game /tmp/chimpmonk-scene-file-bench.hl. Compile source: haxe -cp . -cp example/src -main SceneFileBench -hl /tmp/chimpmonk-scene-file-bench.hl in the ChimpMonk checkout. The source contains 64 warm reads and seven interleaved windows of 128 operations per serialization arm, using example/assets/scenes/cape-crowd.json; no model asset loading occurs in the timed benchmark.\n\nThe allocation-free mixed SceneBench completes under ASH_GC_TLAB=0 at about 128 MiB and reports exact zero warmed bytes. Therefore the higher RSS observation is on an allocating cold workload. Investigate collection triggers/safepoints on the non-TLAB allocation path, and a precise allocation counter with ordinary GC behavior. Keep the incomplete-run and single-attempt limits explicit; the evidence does not establish why the memory difference occurs.","files":null}]}